  "id": "COMPOUND:15387 - PROTEIN:5796",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a mechanistic link between the compound (1S,13S,16S,18R)-18-methoxy-12,15-dimethyl-5,7-dioxa-12,15-diazapentacyclo[11.7.0.01,16.02,10.04,8]icosa-2,4(8),9,19-tetraen-14-one and CX-1, through a series of target interactions involving members of the Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family. This compound is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including 6-Hydroxy-2-[2-(2-hydroxyphenyl) ethyl]chromone, 2,4-Bis[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-5-methoxy-3-[2-(3-methoxyphenyl)ethyl]phenol, and (2E,4E)-N-isobutylundeca-2,4-dien-8,10-diynamide, all of which are known to interact with CX-1. The consistent presence of the SDR family member as a target across these compounds indicates a potential mechanism of action involving the enzyme's role in metabolic processes. The evidence supports the idea that the compound may act as a substrate or inhibitor of the SDR family, thereby influencing CX-1's function. The high scores in the final_score suggest a robust and reliable relationship, though further validation through experimental studies would be necessary to confirm the exact mechanism and biological relevance.",
